Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] gpio: correct the SPI and UART function select table
 from GP9 up

RP2040 datasheet section 1.4.3 (GPIO Functions, Table 2) assigns the SPI
signals to a repeating group of four pins, RX, CSn, SCK and TX, and the UART
signals to TX, RX, CTS and RTS, so GP10 is SPI1 SCK, GP11 SPI1 TX, GP12
SPI1 RX and GP13 SPI1 CSn. The model's pinMapping rows are right through GP8
and shifted one pin from GP9 on: GP9 is SPI1 SCK where the chip has CSn,
GP10 is SPI1 TX where it has SCK, and so on, with the UART column offset
the same way. PL022 reads that table through OnGpioFunctionSelect to find its
clock, transmit, receive and chip-select pins, so a driver that routes SPI1
to GP10-GP13 as the PicoCalc does gets its serial data on the clock pin and
no clock edges at all. The rows for GP9 to GP29 now follow the datasheet
pattern: SPI0 on GP0-GP7 and GP16-GP23, SPI1 on GP8-GP15 and GP24-GP29,
UART0 on GP0-GP3, GP12-GP19 and GP28-GP29, UART1 on GP4-GP11 and GP20-GP27.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-sonnet-5-5)
